WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.077
- But I gotta tell you
this, 'cause I was like,

00:00:02.077 --> 00:00:03.396
"Oh my God, he's gonna do "The Dance",

00:00:03.396 --> 00:00:05.960
so I'm going through a divorce

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.560
and there's been a lot
of, I don't know, books

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.180
and people always give you stuff to help,

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.370
especially when you have kids and stuff

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.730
and I know that you've
been divorced as well

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.880
and it was like, man, there's
so much shame and guilt

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.110
and everybody kind of sends
you stuff and I was like,

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.790
I was just kind of working through it.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.770
And I couldn't quite
nail down the feeling,

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.690
I was like, you don't want to crap on it,

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.420
like you don't want to say,
that didn't count or matter.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.730
But you don't know what to put in it,

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.170
'cause it didn't work out how you wanted.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.860
And so, anyway, I kid you not,

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:41.180
I was listening to my playlist
and "The Dance" came on.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.250
And I was like, no that's the thing.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.260
- That's it.
- That's it.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.300
So I literally, it's not like
your song, like a rip off,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.470
but I literally wrote this whole thing,

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:51.550
like therapeutically for me

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.700
and it's actually on my next album

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.000
and it's the whole kind of, come around.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.350
Like the little tag part is

00:00:59.508 --> 00:01:01.754
♪ Even though my heart is broken ♪

00:01:01.754 --> 00:01:04.730
♪ It was worth the dance anyway ♪

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.450
And it's like this whole
thing but I was like,

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:09.360
I think what's interesting about it

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.600
is I sang that song from childhood

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.460
and it never hit me.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.090
- That's a great song right there.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.960
- Oh my God.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.492
- That's a character of a great song.

00:01:19.492 --> 00:01:22.280
- And it hit me, I was
literally bawling in my own room

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.492
I was like, I mean it was not so bad!

00:01:24.492 --> 00:01:26.360
It was worth it!

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.290
And I literally was like,

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.900
because it is true, I
think a lot of people

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.236
that go through such a devastating,

00:01:30.236 --> 00:01:32.140
there's a lot of grief
with it, a lot of loss.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.570
And a lot of change, especially with kids.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:37.600
It was one of those things,
like all the books were helpful,

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.410
but it's so funny I guess
because I'm a musician,

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:41.125
but I was listening in my
room and I was just like,

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:43.210
(sobs) and I was listening to "The Dance"

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.500
and that's like the one hook of it,

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.980
but it was like the whole
point, I got the point.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.970
And I think sometimes that's so crazy,

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:54.270
like you don't know that's gonna happen.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.500
And you're like, you've known
this song your entire life

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.953
and you freak out when it
actually is a direct impact.

